2. Definitions

"Software" means the Intergrax source code, documentation, configuration,
examples, and other materials made available in the Official Repository.

"Licensor Materials" means portions of the Software created by Artur
Czarnecki, portions effectively transferred to Artur Czarnecki, and materials
to which Artur Czarnecki holds sufficient rights to license under this
license, excluding third-party components and portions whose copyright is
retained by contributors.

"Licensed Materials" means:

(a) Licensor Materials; and

(b) Code Contributions and Documentation Contributions that the Licensor
is authorized to sublicense under Section 8,

excluding third-party components to the extent governed by their own licenses.

"Licensor" means Artur Czarnecki.

"Evaluation" means technical analysis, local testing, proof paths, benchmarks,
experiments, integration assessment, partnership-fit assessment, and
preparation of a Code Contribution or Documentation Contribution, each in a
non-production Evaluation Environment.

"Evaluation Participant" means an individual, employee, contractor, adviser,
or technical reviewer acting solely for Evaluation in a controlled
non-production Evaluation Environment.

"Evaluation Environment" means a local or otherwise isolated non-production
environment used solely for Evaluation. Evaluation Participants may install,
run, test, review code, conduct integration proofs, and perform controlled
technical pilots in an Evaluation Environment. An Evaluation Environment may
not provide an operational service, support an ongoing business process, serve
real customers, process production data except appropriately anonymized or
synthetic test data, replace a production tool, or generate customer-facing
output.

"Production Use" means use of the Software to support real users, customers,
organizations, business processes, production data, or operational services.
Providing the Software as an operational or business service to employees is
Production Use. Employees, contractors, or advisers acting solely as Evaluation
Participants in a controlled non-production Evaluation Environment are not
treated as production users. Running local tests, benchmarks, or documented
evaluation workloads in an Evaluation Environment is not Production Use.

"Commercial Use" means use of the Software directly or indirectly in connection
with revenue generation, paid services, product sales, hosting, consulting
based on a running Intergrax deployment, offering Intergrax to customers, or
incorporating the Software into a commercial product or service. Internal,
non-production Evaluation by a commercial organization is not Commercial Use
solely because the organization is commercial.

"Code Contribution" means code, a patch, pull request, test, configuration,
file, or other technical material that a contributor clearly submits or offers
for inclusion in Intergrax.

"Documentation Contribution" means documentation, a diagram, example,
tutorial, technical description, or other textual or visual material that a
contributor clearly offers for inclusion in Intergrax.

"Feedback" means issue comments, suggestions, opinions, bug reports, feature
proposals, observations, architecture comments, and other feedback that is not
clearly offered for direct inclusion as a project file or material.

"Official Repository" means the public Intergrax repository maintained by the
Licensor at https://github.com/jakbuczarnecki/intergrax and successor
locations designated by the Licensor.

"Authorized Fork" means a public or private fork of the Official Repository
created for Evaluation, code review, discussion, or preparation of a Code
Contribution or Documentation Contribution that retains this LICENSE, retains
copyright notices, is not presented as an official release, is not an
independent distribution, and is not used for Production Use or Commercial
Use.

